# Gallery strip contract (card vs PDP)

**RCA:** `docs/ai/GALLERY_RETURN_TO_MAIN_RCA.md`

## Canon

| Surface | Strip builder | Return-to-main |
|---------|---------------|----------------|
| Catalog **card** | `buildGalleryStripUrls` (main first) | Click main thumb |
| **PDP** (core / generic / Oliver default) | `buildPdpThumbStripUrls` (extras only) | Re-click active extra; lightbox; Oliver color-hero pair may include main |
| Rail visibility | `shouldShowBuyerGalleryRail` / `resolveBuyerGalleryThumbStrip` — show when ≥ 1 photo (single-photo SKUs included). Multi-photo PDP stays extras-only; single-photo PDP falls back to main as the only thumb. | Never gate PDP on extras-only strip length alone for multi-photo |

## Do not

- Put main into every multi-photo PDP strip to “fix” return-to-main (reads as duplicate)
- Hide the rail for single-photo products (`length > 1` gate) — operator rejected that
- Use `showThumbRow = visibleStrip.length > 1` on extras-only PDP strips (hides 2-photo SKUs)
- Claim `:3002` verified without `yarn build:qa` after gallery edits
- Ship gallery strip changes without `yarn test:gallery-contract`
